4306	///     so it holds less scrollback per pool item. Heap pages keep all
4307	///     their rows, but each is its own allocation that `grow` can't
4308	///     reuse in place. On styled output that meant hundreds of times
4309	///     more allocations for about the same scrollback per byte.
4310	///   - A tall terminal may need more trimmed pages to hold its active
4311	///     area than the minimum byte limit allows (see `Limits.minMaxSize`).
